 "caution_items": [
  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "0.7 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 124,201 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "98,207 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, epo_newscrawl_2017_1M, 22.0 million words); 25,994 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words (288 probable English words were removed). Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  }
